00:11:00.706 --> 00:11:03.786
But I mean, even with her relationships

00:11:03.786 --> 00:11:07.546
and her highly targeted 0.70 request,

00:11:07.586 --> 00:11:09.466
a letter is just a piece of paper.

00:11:09.466 --> 00:11:11.386
You need an institutional engine

00:11:11.386 --> 00:11:13.586
to actually drive this through the bureaucracy.

00:11:13.586 --> 00:11:15.666
You need a machine that operates daily.

00:11:15.666 --> 00:11:17.346
And that was PRFAA,

00:11:17.346 --> 00:11:19.666
the Puerto Rico Federal Affairs Administration.

00:11:19.666 --> 00:11:22.226
I really want to dig into the operational mechanics here

00:11:22.226 --> 00:11:24.466
because we always hear the term coalition building,

00:11:24.466 --> 00:11:27.786
but it usually just means putting 50 logos on a PDF

00:11:27.786 --> 00:11:28.666
and calling it a day.

00:11:28.666 --> 00:11:30.386
Yeah, that's standard DC stuff.

00:11:30.386 --> 00:11:33.426
Right, but PRFAA did something completely different.

00:11:33.426 --> 00:11:35.266
Executive Director Gabriela Bafeli

00:11:35.266 --> 00:11:37.826
and Deputy Director Natalia Gandia

00:11:37.826 --> 00:11:40.106
essentially built a localized state department

00:11:40.106 --> 00:11:42.186
combined with a tactical lobbying firm.

00:11:42.186 --> 00:11:46.426
Because they had a highly complex ecosystem to manage.

00:11:46.426 --> 00:11:48.466
The private healthcare sector in Puerto Rico,

00:11:48.466 --> 00:11:52.346
the hospitals, the IPAs, the health plans,

00:11:52.346 --> 00:11:55.186
the community pharmacies, they aren't new to this.

00:11:55.186 --> 00:11:56.946
No, they've been dealing with this for a long time.

00:11:56.946 --> 00:11:58.306
Over 15 years,

00:11:58.306 --> 00:12:00.226
they've been fighting this funding disparity

00:12:00.226 --> 00:12:01.306
for over 15 years.

00:12:01.306 --> 00:12:03.586
So they have immense institutional memory

00:12:03.866 --> 00:12:06.346
and massive amounts of localized data.

00:12:06.346 --> 00:12:08.666
But raw data is heavy and it's hard to move.

00:12:08.666 --> 00:12:12.426
Exactly, PRFAA's job was to act as the operational bridge.

00:12:12.426 --> 00:12:14.226
They channeled all of that localized energy

00:12:14.226 --> 00:12:15.266
from the private sector

00:12:15.266 --> 00:12:18.026
into a single unified laser beam

00:12:18.026 --> 00:12:22.586
aimed directly at the 0.704 request.

00:12:22.586 --> 00:12:24.586
So what does that actually look like on the ground in DC?

00:12:24.586 --> 00:12:26.306
Because I imagine it's not just setting up

00:12:26.306 --> 00:12:28.666
a few cocktail hours and handing out pamphlets.

00:12:28.666 --> 00:12:31.826
Far from it, it is a grueling logistical grind.

00:12:31.826 --> 00:12:33.546
You're talking about Bafeli and Gandia

00:12:33.546 --> 00:12:35.386
coordinating rolling fly-ins.

00:12:35.386 --> 00:12:38.266
They are constantly looking at the congressional calendar.

00:12:38.266 --> 00:12:40.186
They are sequencing the Hill visits.

00:12:40.186 --> 00:12:42.306
They are prepping the private sector leaders

00:12:42.306 --> 00:12:43.946
before they ever set foot

00:12:43.946 --> 00:12:45.906
in a Rayburn office building suite.

00:12:45.906 --> 00:12:48.226
They're essentially casting the meetings.

00:12:48.226 --> 00:12:51.266
Precisely, it's incredibly tactical.

00:12:51.266 --> 00:12:54.426
If they secure a meeting with a mainland representative

00:12:54.426 --> 00:12:57.426
who has a strong voting record on small business issues,

00:12:57.426 --> 00:13:00.826
PRFAA doesn't send the hospital CEO.

00:13:00.826 --> 00:13:02.706
Oh, they send the independent pharmacy owner.

00:13:02.706 --> 00:13:03.746
Exactly.

00:13:03.746 --> 00:13:05.906
And if the representative sits on a committee

00:13:05.906 --> 00:13:08.706
dealing with institutional health care resilience,

00:13:08.706 --> 00:13:10.946
well, then they send the hospital administrators.

00:13:10.946 --> 00:13:11.826
That is so smart.

00:13:11.826 --> 00:13:15.306
They match the exact endpoint of the health care supply chain

00:13:15.306 --> 00:13:17.546
to the specific political interest of the lawmaker.

00:13:17.546 --> 00:13:18.746
And they back it up

00:13:18.746 --> 00:13:21.386
with constant relentless follow-up,

00:13:21.386 --> 00:13:22.986
the rapid debriefs in the hallway

00:13:22.986 --> 00:13:24.346
right after the meeting,

00:13:24.346 --> 00:13:27.106
the technical support for the legislative assistance,

00:13:27.106 --> 00:13:29.866
the signature tracking for the eventual August letter.

00:13:29.866 --> 00:13:32.426
They kept the entire private sector perfectly aligned

00:13:32.426 --> 00:13:33.826
with the governor's strategy.

00:13:33.826 --> 00:13:38.466
Total alignment, no rogue requests, no mixed messaging.

00:13:38.466 --> 00:13:40.346
Just, we have five-star quality.

00:13:40.346 --> 00:13:42.186
We have a 41% funding deficit

00:13:42.186 --> 00:13:46.426
and we need the 0.70 floor in 2028.

00:13:46.426 --> 00:13:51.146
But the true genius of PRFAA strategy

00:13:51.146 --> 00:13:53.866
wasn't just in the DC office, that's right.

00:13:53.866 --> 00:13:56.266
It was getting the lawmakers out of DC

00:13:56.266 --> 00:13:58.306
and putting them on the ground in Puerto Rico.

00:13:58.306 --> 00:13:59.706
Yes.

00:13:59.706 --> 00:14:01.746
Because I understand getting politicians into a room,

00:14:01.746 --> 00:14:04.066
but how do you actually show them a formula

00:14:04.066 --> 00:14:05.866
failing in real time?

00:14:05.866 --> 00:14:08.186
Like a hospital tour usually just involves

00:14:08.186 --> 00:14:09.586
shaking hands with administrators,

00:14:09.586 --> 00:14:11.666
looking at an MRI machine and taking a photo.

00:14:11.666 --> 00:14:13.106
Yeah, the classic photo op.

00:14:13.106 --> 00:14:13.946
Right.

00:14:13.946 --> 00:14:15.666
So why did these specific visits

00:14:15.666 --> 00:14:16.746
actually move the needle

00:14:16.746 --> 00:14:18.546
for deeply skeptical Republicans?

00:14:18.546 --> 00:14:20.906
By exposing them to the actual operating system.

00:14:20.906 --> 00:14:22.626
This wasn't a standard PR tour.

00:14:22.626 --> 00:14:24.306
The internal dossier maps this out

00:14:24.306 --> 00:14:25.586
as a four-doors strategy.

00:14:25.586 --> 00:14:26.426
Okay, four doors.

00:14:26.426 --> 00:14:27.266
They didn't just show them

00:14:27.266 --> 00:14:29.106
the glossy administrative suite.

00:14:29.106 --> 00:14:31.946
They walked them through the harsh economic reality

00:14:31.946 --> 00:14:32.826
of the supply chain.

00:14:32.826 --> 00:14:33.786
Let's look at this sequence,

00:14:33.786 --> 00:14:35.186
starting with the macro view.

00:14:35.186 --> 00:14:36.586
The policy and chamber door?

00:14:36.586 --> 00:14:37.426
Right.

00:14:37.426 --> 00:14:39.626
This was with Luís Luigi Pizarro

00:14:39.626 --> 00:14:41.986
at the Puerto Rico Chamber of Commerce Health

00:14:41.986 --> 00:14:43.466
and Insurance Conferences.

00:14:43.466 --> 00:14:44.906
Okay, so that's the big picture.

00:14:44.906 --> 00:14:45.866
Exactly.

00:14:45.866 --> 00:14:49.466
This is where you establish the systemic stakes.

00:14:49.466 --> 00:14:51.186
You put the lawmakers in a room

00:14:51.186 --> 00:14:53.586
with the island's economic leadership

00:14:53.586 --> 00:14:57.786
to show that this $730 MA benchmark

00:14:57.826 --> 00:14:59.906
isn't just an insurance issue.

00:14:59.906 --> 00:15:03.106
It's a massive overarching economic drag.

00:15:03.106 --> 00:15:04.706
Because it impacts employment

00:15:04.706 --> 00:15:06.066
and capital investment

00:15:06.066 --> 00:15:07.386
and the broader tax base.

00:15:07.386 --> 00:15:08.226
Exactly.

00:15:08.226 --> 00:15:09.986
Okay, so they established the macro,

00:15:09.986 --> 00:15:11.786
then they take them through the second door,

00:15:11.786 --> 00:15:13.266
the hospital door,

00:15:13.266 --> 00:15:14.786
with Dr. Leo Valentin

00:15:14.786 --> 00:15:16.706
at Professional Hospital of Guainabbo.

00:15:16.706 --> 00:15:18.426
And here, the theoretical deficit

00:15:18.426 --> 00:15:20.146
becomes totally tangible.

00:15:20.146 --> 00:15:21.586
When you are underfunded

00:15:21.586 --> 00:15:24.066
by $500 per patient per month,

00:15:24.066 --> 00:15:25.666
what does that actually look like

00:15:25.666 --> 00:15:26.946
on a hospital floor?

00:15:26.946 --> 00:15:28.026
It looks like an inability

00:15:28.026 --> 00:15:29.826
to match mainland nursing salaries.

00:15:29.826 --> 00:15:32.306
Right, which leads to a brutal brain drain.

00:15:32.306 --> 00:15:34.266
It looks like delayed capital expenditures

00:15:34.266 --> 00:15:35.586
for surgical equipment.

00:15:35.586 --> 00:15:36.426
Lawmakers got to see

00:15:36.426 --> 00:15:37.946
that the hospital isn't just complaining

00:15:37.946 --> 00:15:39.266
about profit margins.

00:15:39.266 --> 00:15:40.506
They're literally fighting

00:15:40.506 --> 00:15:42.146
to maintain institutional delivery

00:15:42.146 --> 00:15:44.346
under a crushing financial handicap.

00:15:44.346 --> 00:15:45.186
Wow.

00:15:45.186 --> 00:15:46.826
And then we move to the third door,

00:15:46.826 --> 00:15:47.866
which is fascinating

00:15:47.866 --> 00:15:50.706
because it deals with the actual mechanics of MA care,

00:15:50.706 --> 00:15:52.906
the physician and IPA door.

00:15:52.906 --> 00:15:54.666
This was with Dr. Huaco Vargas

00:15:54.666 --> 00:15:55.866
at Varmed Health Center.

00:15:55.986 --> 00:15:57.506
And this is where the five-star metric

00:15:57.506 --> 00:15:58.786
is actually achieved.

00:15:58.786 --> 00:15:59.906
Oh, this is the ground level.

00:15:59.906 --> 00:16:00.466
Right.

00:16:00.466 --> 00:16:02.666
Lawmakers got to see firsthand

00:16:02.666 --> 00:16:06.226
how independent practice associations or IPAs

00:16:06.226 --> 00:16:07.546
utilize capitation

00:16:07.546 --> 00:16:09.826
and heavily coordinated care models

00:16:09.826 --> 00:16:12.306
to manage chronically ill populations.

00:16:12.306 --> 00:16:14.546
So they saw the aggressive preventative care.

00:16:14.546 --> 00:16:15.226
Yes.

00:16:15.226 --> 00:16:16.986
And the complex referral management

00:16:16.986 --> 00:16:19.466
that keeps readmissions so low.

00:16:19.466 --> 00:16:21.866
They saw why the quality is so high,

00:16:21.866 --> 00:16:23.026
but they also saw

00:16:23.026 --> 00:16:25.026
how the underlying funding starvation

00:16:25.066 --> 00:16:27.266
severely restricts the resources

00:16:27.266 --> 00:16:29.066
those primary care doctors have

00:16:29.066 --> 00:16:30.826
to actually manage that patient load.

00:16:30.826 --> 00:16:31.386
Precisely.

00:16:31.386 --> 00:16:32.826
It made the contradiction real.

00:16:32.826 --> 00:16:33.866
But it's the fourth door

00:16:33.866 --> 00:16:34.946
that really seemed to break

00:16:34.946 --> 00:16:37.026
through the partisan resistance,

00:16:37.026 --> 00:16:38.266
the pharmacy door.

00:16:38.266 --> 00:16:40.266
Elliot Pacheco at Súper Farmacia,

00:16:40.266 --> 00:16:41.146
I love Verde.

00:16:41.146 --> 00:16:42.026
I love this part

00:16:42.026 --> 00:16:43.866
because everybody understands a local pharmacy.

00:16:43.866 --> 00:16:45.386
You walk into a community pharmacy

00:16:45.386 --> 00:16:47.946
and you immediately grasp the retail economics.

00:16:47.946 --> 00:16:48.546
Exactly.

00:16:48.546 --> 00:16:50.506
This wasn't some corporate boardroom.

00:16:50.506 --> 00:16:52.786
Lawmakers were standing in a community pharmacy

00:16:52.826 --> 00:16:55.226
looking at the exact cash flow constraints.

00:16:55.226 --> 00:16:57.666
They were seeing the acquisition costs

00:16:57.666 --> 00:16:58.986
of specialty medications,

00:16:58.986 --> 00:17:00.866
the predatory DIR fees,

00:17:00.866 --> 00:17:03.306
the immense squeeze from PBMs.

00:17:03.306 --> 00:17:04.226
Yes.

00:17:04.226 --> 00:17:06.026
When the federal MA benchmark

00:17:06.026 --> 00:17:07.506
is severely depressed,

00:17:07.506 --> 00:17:09.226
the downstream reimbursement rates

00:17:09.226 --> 00:17:11.586
for the pharmacy are razor thin

00:17:11.586 --> 00:17:13.346
or often completely underwater.

00:17:13.346 --> 00:17:15.626
So the pharmacist is literally asking

00:17:15.626 --> 00:17:19.066
if I dispense this insulin to this senior,

00:17:19.066 --> 00:17:20.866
will I lose money on the transaction?

00:17:20.866 --> 00:17:22.346
And when a conservative lawmaker

00:17:22.346 --> 00:17:23.706
sees a small business owner

00:17:23.706 --> 00:17:24.786
and independent pharmacist

00:17:24.786 --> 00:17:26.066
facing an existential threat

00:17:26.066 --> 00:17:28.426
because of a flawed federal algorithm,

00:17:28.426 --> 00:17:29.906
it fundamentally changes

00:17:29.906 --> 00:17:31.346
their political calculus.

00:17:31.346 --> 00:17:32.626
It's not abstract anymore.

00:17:32.626 --> 00:17:33.186
Not at all.

00:17:33.186 --> 00:17:34.986
Which perfectly sets up the centerpiece

00:17:34.986 --> 00:17:36.586
of this entire coalition.

00:17:36.586 --> 00:17:39.066
The white whale of their advocacy strategy,

00:17:39.066 --> 00:17:40.386
Representative Greg Murphy.

00:17:40.386 --> 00:17:43.066
His conversion is the defining political achievement

00:17:43.066 --> 00:17:44.346
of this entire campaign.

00:17:44.346 --> 00:17:45.746
Because if you look at the landscape

00:17:45.746 --> 00:17:46.986
in early 2024,

00:17:46.986 --> 00:17:49.546
Greg Murphy is the absolute last guy

00:17:49.546 --> 00:17:51.266
you would expect to lead a coalition

00:17:51.266 --> 00:17:52.906
defending Medicare Advantage funding.

00:17:52.906 --> 00:17:54.466
The absolute last.

00:17:54.466 --> 00:17:56.586
In March 2024, he goes on the record,

00:17:56.586 --> 00:17:58.066
completely unvarnished,

00:17:58.066 --> 00:17:59.426
saying he is, quote,

00:17:59.426 --> 00:18:01.706
personally not a fan of MA.

00:18:01.706 --> 00:18:03.186
He basically suggests the program

00:18:03.186 --> 00:18:05.546
needs to be abolished and restarted from scratch.

00:18:05.546 --> 00:18:07.826
Which raises an important question, right.

00:18:07.826 --> 00:18:09.986
Why would PRFAA and the governor

00:18:09.986 --> 00:18:12.666
waste their time on one of the most outspoken critics

00:18:12.666 --> 00:18:14.826
of national Medicare Advantage abuses?

00:18:14.826 --> 00:18:15.906
Seriously.

00:18:15.906 --> 00:18:17.066
If I'm running this campaign,

00:18:17.066 --> 00:18:19.666
I'm looking for members who already love MA.

00:18:19.706 --> 00:18:22.066
Why target the guy trying to burn it down?

00:18:22.066 --> 00:18:23.506
Because of his background.

00:18:23.506 --> 00:18:25.666
Representative Murphy is a physician.

00:18:25.666 --> 00:18:26.666
Ah, right.

00:18:26.666 --> 00:18:28.546
He understands clinical reality

00:18:28.546 --> 00:18:30.546
versus administrative bloat.

00:18:30.546 --> 00:18:33.706
His deep skepticism of MA wasn't arbitrary.

00:18:33.706 --> 00:18:36.026
It was rooted in highly valid criticisms

00:18:36.026 --> 00:18:37.826
of the massive national carriers.

00:18:37.826 --> 00:18:40.786
He was frustrated by the aggressive prior authorizations,

00:18:40.786 --> 00:18:42.426
the systemic denial of care.

00:18:42.426 --> 00:18:43.266
Exactly.

00:18:43.266 --> 00:18:44.826
The aggressive coding intensity

00:18:44.826 --> 00:18:47.626
and the massive profit margins of national insurers

00:18:47.626 --> 00:18:50.066
at the expense of actual patient care.

00:18:50.066 --> 00:18:52.706
Which, to be fair, are the exact things

00:18:52.706 --> 00:18:55.226
most people hate about the corporatization of healthcare.

00:18:55.226 --> 00:18:56.066
Right.

00:18:56.066 --> 00:18:59.026
But in April 2025, Murphy takes the trip.

00:18:59.026 --> 00:19:00.906
He speaks alongside Luigi Pizarro

00:19:00.906 --> 00:19:02.466
at the chamber conference.

00:19:02.466 --> 00:19:04.866
He goes to professional hospital Guainabo

00:19:04.866 --> 00:19:06.186
with Dr. Valentin.

00:19:06.186 --> 00:19:07.626
He sees the IPA model

00:19:07.626 --> 00:19:09.226
ad-varmed with Dr. Vargas.

00:19:09.226 --> 00:19:11.546
And he stands in Super Formatia, Ayla Verde,

00:19:11.546 --> 00:19:13.426
talking directly with Elliot Pacheco

00:19:13.426 --> 00:19:15.146
and other independent pharmacy owners.

00:19:15.146 --> 00:19:16.986
He goes through the four doors.

00:19:16.986 --> 00:19:18.706
And because he's a doctor,

00:19:18.706 --> 00:19:20.666
he isn't just looking at the spreadsheets.

00:19:20.666 --> 00:19:22.666
He is looking at the clinical pathways.

00:19:22.666 --> 00:19:24.266
He recognizes immediately

00:19:24.266 --> 00:19:27.386
that Puerto Rico's MA market is structurally different

00:19:27.386 --> 00:19:30.026
from the mainland corporate models he despises.

00:19:30.026 --> 00:19:31.146
It is deeply integrated.

00:19:31.146 --> 00:19:34.266
It relies heavily on local independent providers.

00:19:34.266 --> 00:19:35.666
And it is actually delivering

00:19:35.666 --> 00:19:37.666
on the promise of managed care,

00:19:37.666 --> 00:19:41.106
which is evidenced by the 81% five-star enrollment.

00:19:41.106 --> 00:19:42.906
So he realizes that by starting

00:19:42.906 --> 00:19:44.826
the funding formula in Puerto Rico,

00:19:44.826 --> 00:19:46.626
the federal government isn't punishing

00:19:46.626 --> 00:19:49.746
the national corporate executives in their high-rises.

00:19:49.746 --> 00:19:52.266
It is actively crushing Dr. Valentin,

00:19:52.266 --> 00:19:54.506
Dr. Vargas, and Elliot Pacheco.

00:19:54.506 --> 00:19:56.986
It is punishing the exact local providers

00:19:56.986 --> 00:19:58.466
Murphy wants to protect.

00:19:58.466 --> 00:20:00.666
Which leads directly to this watershed moment

00:20:00.666 --> 00:20:02.746
in July 2025.

00:20:02.746 --> 00:20:04.386
During a congressional hearing,

00:20:04.386 --> 00:20:06.066
while still being highly critical

00:20:06.066 --> 00:20:07.986
of national MA carriers,

00:20:07.986 --> 00:20:11.466
Murphy explicitly carves out Puerto Rico.

00:20:11.466 --> 00:20:13.106
He points to their system and says,

00:20:13.106 --> 00:20:14.946
quote, they do it right.

00:20:14.946 --> 00:20:16.266
They do it right.

00:20:16.266 --> 00:20:20.466
That forward sentence is the holy grail for PRFAA.

00:20:20.466 --> 00:20:24.106
It unlocked the entire Republican policy frame.

00:20:24.106 --> 00:20:25.866
So Murphy proved that you can hold

00:20:25.866 --> 00:20:27.746
two thoughts simultaneously.

00:20:27.746 --> 00:20:30.706
You can demand intense accountability from insurers,

00:20:30.706 --> 00:20:33.826
demand massive PBM reform and fight fraud,

00:20:33.826 --> 00:20:35.906
while also demanding that the federal government

00:20:35.906 --> 00:20:37.946
provide an adequate baseline of funding

00:20:37.946 --> 00:20:40.826
to protect local providers and patient choice.

00:20:40.826 --> 00:20:42.786
Right, he separated the conduct of bad actors

00:20:42.786 --> 00:20:44.306
from the underlying payment methodology.

00:20:44.306 --> 00:20:45.146
Exactly.

00:20:45.146 --> 00:20:46.546
We'll be very precise here.

00:20:46.546 --> 00:20:47.946
Murphy didn't wake up one morning

00:20:47.946 --> 00:20:50.986
and invent the 0.70 benchmark floor.

00:20:50.986 --> 00:20:52.546
Oh no, not at all.

00:20:52.546 --> 00:20:54.226
He didn't build the actuarial case.

00:20:54.226 --> 00:20:56.826
PRFAA, the governor and the private sector

00:20:56.826 --> 00:20:58.666
spent years building the engine,

00:20:58.666 --> 00:21:01.106
refining the fuel and mapping the destination.

00:21:01.106 --> 00:21:03.266
Murphy was the key turning the ignition.

00:21:03.266 --> 00:21:06.066
He provided the uniquely credible validation.

00:21:06.066 --> 00:21:08.346
Yeah, when the guy who hates MA

00:21:08.346 --> 00:21:10.506
tells the rest of the Republican caucus,

00:21:10.506 --> 00:21:12.706
actually we need to protect MA funding

00:21:12.706 --> 00:21:14.746
in this specific jurisdiction.

00:21:14.746 --> 00:21:16.386
Everyone else stops and listens.

00:21:16.386 --> 00:21:18.266
It gives them permission to support it.

00:21:18.266 --> 00:21:20.706
But one guy, even a highly credible one,

00:21:20.706 --> 00:21:21.906
isn't a coalition.

00:21:21.906 --> 00:21:23.946
You don't move the HHS secretary

00:21:23.946 --> 00:21:26.066
or the CMS actuaries with one signature.

00:21:26.066 --> 00:21:27.146
No, you need numbers.

00:21:27.146 --> 00:21:30.226
So PRFAA leverages Murphy's conversion

00:21:30.226 --> 00:21:31.946
and starts bringing in different facets

00:21:31.946 --> 00:21:34.026
of the GOP conference.

00:21:34.026 --> 00:21:37.146
Let's look at representative Buddy Carter from Georgia

00:21:37.146 --> 00:21:38.826
because he brings an entirely different

00:21:38.826 --> 00:21:41.066
microscopic lens to this problem.

00:21:41.066 --> 00:21:43.426
Carter is fascinating because he isn't looking

00:21:43.426 --> 00:21:46.466
at this primarily through the physician lens, like Murphy.

00:21:46.466 --> 00:21:49.306
He is looking at it through the retail pharmacy lens.

00:21:49.306 --> 00:21:50.066
Right.

00:21:50.066 --> 00:21:53.786
Carter owned an independent pharmacy for 32 years.

00:21:53.786 --> 00:21:56.066
He is arguably the most aggressive critic

00:21:56.066 --> 00:21:57.866
of PBMs in Congress.

00:21:57.866 --> 00:22:00.626
So when PRFAA gets Carter down to Puerto Rico

00:22:00.626 --> 00:22:03.186
in April, 2026, they know exactly

00:22:03.186 --> 00:22:04.586
which door matters most for him.

00:22:04.586 --> 00:22:06.466
They take him straight to Super Formatia,

00:22:06.466 --> 00:22:08.626
Isla Verde, to meet with Elia Pacheco.

00:22:08.626 --> 00:22:10.866
And it's not a politician talking to an constituent.

00:22:10.866 --> 00:22:12.506
It's an owner talking to an owner.

00:22:12.506 --> 00:22:15.466
They speak the exact same highly technical language

00:22:15.466 --> 00:22:18.866
of dispensing fees, clawbacks, and working capital.

00:22:18.866 --> 00:22:20.306
Carter intrinsically understands

00:22:20.306 --> 00:22:24.066
that when the federal benchmark drops to $730,

00:22:24.066 --> 00:22:26.026
the PBMs don't absorb that loss.

00:22:26.026 --> 00:22:27.066
Oh, of course not.

00:22:27.066 --> 00:22:29.026
They push the pain downstream

00:22:29.026 --> 00:22:30.706
to the independent pharmacist.

00:22:30.706 --> 00:22:32.986
So Carter signs onto the coalition

00:22:32.986 --> 00:22:34.986
and he brings this massive credibility

00:22:34.986 --> 00:22:38.546
regarding small business protection and PBM reform.

00:22:38.546 --> 00:22:41.226
The argument is just getting wider and wider.

00:22:41.226 --> 00:22:42.146
Then you look at someone like

00:22:42.146 --> 00:22:44.546
Representative Gus Bilorakis from Florida.

00:22:44.546 --> 00:22:46.306
Why is he so critical?

00:22:46.306 --> 00:22:48.666
Continuity and deep historical ties.

00:22:48.666 --> 00:22:49.506
Okay.

00:22:49.506 --> 00:22:52.226
Bilorakis had a documented legislative partnership

00:22:52.226 --> 00:22:55.066
with Governor Gonzales Cologne on territorial health care

00:22:55.066 --> 00:22:56.786
that predates Hurricane Maria.

00:22:56.786 --> 00:22:58.386
Wow, so he goes way back.

00:22:58.386 --> 00:23:00.386
He represents the institutional memory

00:23:00.386 --> 00:23:02.386
of Puerto Rico's health care struggles.

00:23:02.386 --> 00:23:05.026
And he brought this fascinating symbolic element

00:23:05.026 --> 00:23:08.626
to the fight with the Roberto Clemente statue bill

00:23:08.626 --> 00:23:10.626
in August, 2026.

00:23:10.666 --> 00:23:13.266
It's a brilliant piece of legislative signaling.

00:23:13.266 --> 00:23:14.626
Now the dossier acknowledges

00:23:14.626 --> 00:23:17.386
that a statue doesn't change actuarial policy,

00:23:17.386 --> 00:23:19.826
but rhetorically it perfectly frames

00:23:19.826 --> 00:23:22.106
Puerto Rico's entire argument.

00:23:22.106 --> 00:23:25.146
The Clemente statue is about recognizing excellence,

00:23:25.146 --> 00:23:26.946
service, and high performance

00:23:26.946 --> 00:23:29.146
despite overwhelming adversity.

00:23:29.146 --> 00:23:30.646
Right, they aren't coming to Washington

00:23:30.646 --> 00:23:32.026
with their hands out saying,

00:23:32.026 --> 00:23:34.186
we are failing, please bail us out.

00:23:34.186 --> 00:23:35.146
Exactly.

00:23:35.146 --> 00:23:36.866
They're coming to Washington saying,

00:23:36.866 --> 00:23:38.386
we are the best in the country.

00:23:38.386 --> 00:23:40.306
We are delivering five star results

00:23:40.306 --> 00:23:42.506
under a benchmark that would completely bankrupt

00:23:42.506 --> 00:23:45.186
a mainland hospital, reward the excellence.

00:23:45.186 --> 00:23:47.426
And that framing appeals immensely

00:23:47.426 --> 00:23:51.186
to the merit-based philosophy of the Republican conference,

00:23:51.186 --> 00:23:54.026
which is why you see the coalition expand to 14 members

00:23:54.026 --> 00:23:56.466
by the August 3, 2026 letter.

00:23:56.466 --> 00:23:58.386
It's an incredibly diverse group too.

00:23:58.386 --> 00:24:00.266
You have Brian Fitzpatrick from Pennsylvania

00:24:00.266 --> 00:24:02.986
bringing continuity on the physician migration crisis.

00:24:02.986 --> 00:24:04.426
Don Bacon from Nebraska.

00:24:04.426 --> 00:24:05.786
And why does Nebraska care?

00:24:05.786 --> 00:24:07.146
Right, why Nebraska?

00:24:07.146 --> 00:24:08.826
Because Bacon realizes that

00:24:08.826 --> 00:24:11.426
as MA penetration climbs in the Midwest,

00:24:11.426 --> 00:24:14.026
this exact FFS data corruption

00:24:14.026 --> 00:24:15.626
is gonna hit his state eventually.

00:24:15.626 --> 00:24:16.546
He sees the future.

00:24:16.546 --> 00:24:18.626
You also have the territorial perspective

00:24:18.626 --> 00:24:21.066
from Amua Amada Ridewagon of American Samoa

00:24:21.066 --> 00:24:22.826
and James Moylan from Guam.

00:24:22.826 --> 00:24:24.346
Plus the Florida heavyweights, right?

00:24:24.346 --> 00:24:25.266
Oh.

00:24:25.266 --> 00:24:28.026
Carlos Kimenez, Maria Elvira Salazar,

00:24:28.026 --> 00:24:29.306
Mario Diaz Ballart.

00:24:29.306 --> 00:24:32.306
Who deeply understand the senior care demographic

00:24:32.306 --> 00:24:34.306
and the Puerto Rican migration link.

00:24:34.306 --> 00:24:36.626
And then you have members like Pete Sessions,

00:24:36.626 --> 00:24:39.226
Mike Kelly, Riley Moore and Claudia Tenney.

00:24:39.226 --> 00:24:41.826
14 Republicans all signing on

00:24:41.826 --> 00:24:44.666
to Governor Gonzalez-Colon's exact request,

00:24:44.666 --> 00:24:48.946
establish a 70% national minimum MA benchmark floor

00:24:48.946 --> 00:24:50.226
beginning in 2028.

00:24:50.226 --> 00:24:52.466
I mean, it is a massive political victory.

00:24:52.466 --> 00:24:55.866
It is, but as any seasoned DC operative will tell you,

00:24:55.866 --> 00:24:58.066
a political victory is just the prerequisite

00:24:58.066 --> 00:24:59.826
for the actual administrative war.

00:24:59.826 --> 00:25:01.386
Right, because you can have the letter,

00:25:01.386 --> 00:25:02.226
you can have the governor,

00:25:02.226 --> 00:25:03.826
you can have the 14 members.

00:25:03.826 --> 00:25:06.586
But Greg Murphy doesn't write the code

00:25:06.586 --> 00:25:08.066
for the CMS payment algorithms.

00:25:08.066 --> 00:25:08.906
No, he does not.

00:25:08.906 --> 00:25:09.826
The fight isn't over.

00:25:09.826 --> 00:25:10.826
What are the next steps?

00:25:10.826 --> 00:25:13.346
Do they just sit back and wait for HHS to cut the check?

00:25:13.346 --> 00:25:14.386
Not even close.

00:25:14.386 --> 00:25:16.786
The pressure campaign now has to transition

00:25:16.786 --> 00:25:19.546
into the labyrinth of administrative rulemaking.

00:25:19.546 --> 00:25:21.786
The immediate next steps require the governor,

00:25:21.786 --> 00:25:24.426
PRFAA and the private sector

00:25:24.426 --> 00:25:26.906
to sustain intense technical engagement

00:25:26.906 --> 00:25:30.306
with HHS, CMS, congressional leadership,

00:25:30.306 --> 00:25:32.906
relevant committees and the White House.

00:25:32.906 --> 00:25:34.706
They have to convince the actuaries.

00:25:34.706 --> 00:25:36.266
Crucially, yes.

00:25:36.266 --> 00:25:39.146
The career officials in the CMS office of the actuary,

00:25:39.146 --> 00:25:41.346
the people in the basement who actually calculate

00:25:41.346 --> 00:25:44.986
the geographic practice cost index and those FFS baseline.

00:25:44.986 --> 00:25:46.386
The ones actually doing the math.

00:25:46.386 --> 00:25:49.026
Right, PRFAA has to prove to them

00:25:49.026 --> 00:25:50.506
not only that the math is broken,

00:25:50.506 --> 00:25:53.626
but that CMS possesses the explicit legal authority

00:25:53.626 --> 00:25:57.666
likely through section 1876A of the Social Security Act

00:25:57.666 --> 00:26:01.906
or similar adjustment levers to implement the 0.70 floor

00:26:01.906 --> 00:26:03.826
without requiring new legislation.

00:26:03.826 --> 00:26:05.666
So it shifts from a political argument

00:26:05.666 --> 00:26:08.546
to a deeply technical, legal and statistical argument.

00:26:08.546 --> 00:26:09.546
Completely.

00:26:09.546 --> 00:26:12.466
They have to keep the 14-member coalition engaged,

00:26:12.466 --> 00:26:14.026
keep the private sector aligned,

00:26:14.026 --> 00:26:16.906
and guide this all the way to the 2028 rate announcement.

00:26:16.906 --> 00:26:19.026
It requires just relentless vigilance.

00:26:19.026 --> 00:26:19.866
It really does.

00:26:19.866 --> 00:26:22.826
Okay, we have covered an immense amount of ground today,

00:26:22.826 --> 00:26:25.746
from the math of the CMSR ratings

00:26:25.746 --> 00:26:28.906
to the granular logistics of congressional fly-ins.

00:26:28.906 --> 00:26:30.506
Let's pull this all together.

00:26:30.506 --> 00:26:32.306
Puerto Rico built the case.

00:26:32.306 --> 00:26:35.666
They had the decades of localized private sector knowledge

00:26:35.666 --> 00:26:39.546
and the undeniable 81% five-star quality data.

00:26:39.546 --> 00:26:42.306
And Governor Gonzales Cologne took that raw data

00:26:42.306 --> 00:26:44.346
and engineered a highly specific

00:26:44.346 --> 00:26:46.706
legally viable policy objective,

00:26:46.706 --> 00:26:49.666
the 0.70 benchmark floor.

00:26:49.666 --> 00:26:52.186
And PRFAA built the coalition.

00:26:52.186 --> 00:26:54.466
They managed the logistical ground game,

00:26:54.466 --> 00:26:55.706
channeled the private sector

00:26:55.706 --> 00:26:57.506
through the four doors of exposure,

00:26:57.506 --> 00:27:00.386
and strategically deployed that reality to lawmakers.

00:27:00.386 --> 00:27:02.906
Greg Murphy provided the essential credibility

00:27:02.906 --> 00:27:05.426
by proving you can fight national corporate abuses

00:27:05.426 --> 00:27:07.866
while still defending local private sector delivery.

00:27:07.866 --> 00:27:10.946
And the 14 Republicans provided the political mass necessary

00:27:10.946 --> 00:27:13.186
to force the administration's hand,

00:27:13.186 --> 00:27:14.906
which brings us to the ultimate

00:27:14.906 --> 00:27:17.906
unavoidable conclusion of this entire deep dive.

00:27:17.906 --> 00:27:20.786
The contradiction that Washington can no longer ignore.

00:27:20.786 --> 00:27:23.386
Puerto Rico has already delivered the quality.

00:27:23.386 --> 00:27:28.266
99% in 4.5 stars or higher, 81% in five stars.

00:27:28.266 --> 00:27:31.146
They are dominating the CMS quality metrics.

00:27:31.146 --> 00:27:34.626
And Washington has consistently delivered the underfunding,

00:27:34.626 --> 00:27:39.626
a $730 benchmark against a $1,246 national average.

00:27:40.466 --> 00:27:42.426
In a purely merit-based system,

00:27:42.426 --> 00:27:44.466
especially under a Republican administration

00:27:44.466 --> 00:27:46.346
that claims to reward performance,

00:27:46.346 --> 00:27:48.106
efficiency and results,

00:27:48.106 --> 00:27:51.586
those two outcomes simply cannot logically coexist.

00:27:51.586 --> 00:27:54.106
They are mutually exclusive concepts.

00:27:54.106 --> 00:27:56.706
If the federal government's own quality assessment system

00:27:56.706 --> 00:27:58.426
declares that Puerto Rico is operating

00:27:58.426 --> 00:28:01.186
at the absolute pinnacle of healthcare excellence,

00:28:01.186 --> 00:28:03.986
while its own actuarial payment methodology

00:28:03.986 --> 00:28:06.626
leaves the island starved near the absolute bottom,

00:28:06.626 --> 00:28:08.386
well, the problem is not the providers.

00:28:08.386 --> 00:28:10.426
No, the problem is the formula.

00:28:10.426 --> 00:28:12.586
You could hold the massive insurers accountable.

00:28:12.586 --> 00:28:16.466
You can and must aggressively reform the PBMs.

00:28:16.466 --> 00:28:19.146
You can fight fraud and protect patient choice.

00:28:19.146 --> 00:28:21.266
But ultimately, you have to fix the formula.

00:28:21.266 --> 00:28:23.386
Because of a system that claims to value

00:28:23.386 --> 00:28:26.466
and reward quality continuously punishes

00:28:26.466 --> 00:28:27.866
the one jurisdiction delivering

00:28:27.866 --> 00:28:29.786
the highest quality in the nation,

00:28:29.786 --> 00:28:32.546
that system loses all intellectual

00:28:32.546 --> 00:28:34.746
and functional credibility.

00:28:34.746 --> 00:28:36.586
I'm gonna leave you with a final thought to chew on.

00:28:36.586 --> 00:28:38.266
We started off talking about excellence

00:28:38.266 --> 00:28:40.786
being penalized by a math equation.

00:28:40.786 --> 00:28:42.506
If the federal government can look at a market

00:28:42.506 --> 00:28:45.226
that achieves 81% five-star enrollment,

00:28:45.226 --> 00:28:48.146
look at a local hospital struggling to retain nurses,

00:28:48.146 --> 00:28:50.346
look at an independent pharmacist wondering

00:28:50.346 --> 00:28:52.586
if they can afford to dispense insulin.

00:28:52.586 --> 00:28:54.586
Well, I mean, and then decide to starve

00:28:54.586 --> 00:28:57.626
that entire ecosystem of 41% of its funding

00:28:57.626 --> 00:28:59.826
simply because an outdated corrupted fee

00:28:59.826 --> 00:29:01.586
for service sample dictates it.

00:29:01.586 --> 00:29:03.586
What does they actually say about how our government

00:29:03.586 --> 00:29:05.986
defines the word value in healthcare?

00:29:05.986 --> 00:29:08.546
Are we paying for actual human excellence?

00:29:08.546 --> 00:29:09.866
Or are we just paying for the math

00:29:09.866 --> 00:29:12.186
to look clean on a bureaucrat's spreadsheet?

00:29:12.186 --> 00:29:13.226
Think about that next time you look

00:29:13.226 --> 00:29:14.626
at your own healthcare bill.

